{"strongs": "H0411", "word": "אֵל", "translit": "el", "root": "אל", "morph": "H:DemP", "pos": "pronoun plural masculine & feminine", "gloss": "these", "definition": "I. אֵל pronoun plural masculine & feminine = the more usual אֵלֶּה , these 1Chr 20:8 with article הָאֵל Gen 19:8 ; Gen 19:25 ; Gen 26:3 ; Gen 26:4 ; Gen 7:72 ; Deut 19:11 . (Merely an orthographic variation of אֵלֶּה , and doubtless pronounced similarly; the kindred dialects have in genl. a dissyllabic form: see below אֵלֶּה . Written similarly in Phoenician, e.g. CIS Deut 3:22 ; Deut 14:5 ; Deut 93:3 ( האל ), but ZMG 1875, 240 (Neo-Punic) אלא ; in Plaut. Poen. see I. 9 transliterated ily ; Schroed Phoenician Gr. p. 81, 160, 286 ff. )", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB423')\">BDB423</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H411')\">H411</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB422')\">BDB422</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB424')\">BDB424</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>אֵל</bdbheb> <b>pronoun plural masculine &amp; feminine</b> = the more usual <bdbheb>אֵלֶּה</bdbheb>, <highlight>these</highlight> <ref ref=\"1Chr 20:8\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(13,20,8)\">1Chr 20:8</ref> with article <bdbheb>הָאֵל</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 19:8\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(1,19,8)\">Gen 19:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 19:25\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(1,19,25)\">Gen 19:25</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 26:3\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(1,26,3)\">Gen 26:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 26:4\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(1,26,4)\">Gen 26:4</ref>; <checkingNeeded/><wrongReferenceRemoved/> <checkingNeeded/><wrongReferenceRemoved/> <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Gen 7:72\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"72\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"72\" onclick=\"bcv(1,7,72)\">Gen 7:72</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 19:11\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(5,19,11)\">Deut 19:11</ref>. (Merely an orthographic variation of <bdbheb>אֵלֶּה</bdbheb>, and doubtless pronounced similarly; the kindred dialects have in genl. a dissyllabic form: see below <bdbheb>אֵלֶּה</bdbheb>. Written similarly in Phoenician, e.g. <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('CIS')\">CIS</lookup> <ref ref=\"Deut 3:22\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(5,3,22)\">Deut 3:22</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 14:5\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(5,14,5)\">Deut 14:5</ref>; <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Deut 93:3\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"93\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"93\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(5,93,3)\">Deut 93:3</ref> (<bdbheb>האל</bdbheb>), but <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('ZMG')\">ZMG<sup>1875, 240</sup></lookup> (Neo-Punic) <bdbheb>אלא</bdbheb>; in Plaut. Poen. see I. 9 transliterated <highlight>ily</highlight>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Schröd')\">Schroed<sup>Phoenician Gr. p. 81, 160, 286 ff.</sup></lookup>) </p><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "1Chr 20:8", "book": "1CH", "chapter": 20, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Gen 19:8", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 19, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Gen 19:25", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 19, "verse": 25}, {"raw": "Gen 26:3", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 26, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Gen 26:4", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 26, "verse": 4}, {"raw": "Gen 7:72", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 7, "verse": 72}, {"raw": "Deut 19:11", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 19, "verse": 11}, {"raw": "Deut 3:22", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 3, "verse": 22}, {"raw": "Deut 14:5", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 14, "verse": 5}, {"raw": "Deut 93:3", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 93, "verse": 3}], "flagged": {"hebrew": ["אֵל", "אֵלֶּה", "הָאֵל", "האל", "אלא"], "aramaic": [], "greek": [], "translit": [], "abbreviations": ["CIS", "Schröd", "ZMG"]}, "covers": [], "bdbid": "BDB423", "source": "BDB", "testament": "OT"}